{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EDcWDV9iFpQFBKXnEp6xgH","type":"tool_result","content":"trees are too large to ship as certificates.\n\n\\subsection{A dataset with certified pathwidth}\n\\label{sec:dataset}\n\nSection~\\ref{sec:equiv} showed that one certified pathwidth $w$ answers every\nproblem in the exact core. Pathwidth, vertex separation and the vertex\nseparator game take the value $w$, and MOSP, gate matrix layout with multiple\nfolding, one-dimensional logic, interval thickness, narrowness and node search\ntake $w+1$. We therefore built one dataset from every benchmark collection of\nthose problems that we could obtain, including the MOSP corpus.\n\nThe unit of the dataset is the \\emph{isomorphism class}: the set of instances\none and two wide, and two, PLA folding and edge separation, are false as stated,\nalthough a variant of each is exact (Table~\\ref{tab:master}). Moving between\nthe problems paid twice. Read as a pathwidth algorithm, the best exact\nopen-stacks search turned out to rest on two false dominance theorems, and the\nrule that corrects them was already known in the pathwidth literature. And one\ncertified pathwidth answers every problem in the exact core at once, which is\nwhat made a single dataset for nine problems possible.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d20ab00f-ced5-4701-8f82-053c98f1df8f","uuid":"2810663e-f098-468c-b48b-a4edba34016f","timestamp":"2026-10-06T20:16:27.454Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"trees are too large to ship as certificates.\n\n\\subsection{A dataset with certified pathwidth}\n\\label{sec:dataset}\n\nSection~\\ref{sec:equiv} showed that one certified pathwidth $w$ answers every\nproblem in the exact core. Pathwidth, vertex separation and the vertex\nseparator game take the value $w$, and MOSP, gate matrix layout with multiple\nfolding, one-dimensional logic, interval thickness, narrowness and node search\ntake $w+1$. We therefore built one da